      "id": 1,
      "text": "Zilwaukee sprang in 1848 when brothers Daniel and Solomon Johnson built a saw mill on the Saginaw River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zilwaukee%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Saginaw Jackson & Lansing Railroad finished its line through Zilwaukee on January 7, 1868, linking Chicago to West Bay City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.zilwaukeemichigan.gov/community/schools/zilwaukee-history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Legend says the town’s name was chosen to trick immigrants into thinking they were heading to Milwaukee, Wisconsin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
